# Console-Based Simple Calculator in C

Welcome to my very first official C programming project! This repository marks the beginning of my engineering portfolio as a computer science student.

## Project Overview
This is a menu-driven, command-line calculator built using a `switch-case` architecture in C. Unlike basic tutorials, this implementation features input handling to prevent runtime errors.

###  Key Features
* **Full Arithmetic Suite:** Handles Addition, Subtraction, Multiplication, and Division.
* **Smart Validation:** Features a robust edge-case check to completely prevent **Division by Zero** application crashes.
* **User-Friendly Menu:** Clean, numeric option-based console interface.

To use the Basic Calculator you just need to choose the arithmetic operation you need to do in two numbers.Then you just need to give the input which
means to type the two Numbers one by one and press enter.

